/*
 * Localizable.strings (en) — the UIKit/SwiftUI shell's strings.
 *
 * The keys ARE the English text, so this table is what the app shows when no
 * translation exists and is also the complete list a translator works from.
 * scripts/check-localization.py collects every key the code can look up
 * (OpenQ4_L call sites, the kSettings table, SwiftUI and App Intents literals)
 * and fails if any of the four tables lacks one, maps it differently in en,
 * changes its format specifiers, or carries a key nothing reads.
 *
 * The engine's own strings are NOT here: they are localised upstream in pak0
 * (strings/*.lang, en/fr/it/es) and reached with #str_ ids.
 *
 * D-088 (slice 1, mechanism) and D-112 (slices 2-3: onboarding, row titles,
 * options; the per-option prose too, flagged for a native reader).
 */

